  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Tuesday)\nIssued at 146 PM CDT WED AUG 5 2026\n\nA rather mundane upper-level pattern is anticipated for most of\nthe next seven days, leading to a mostly \"copy/paste\" style\nforecast across the region. By tomorrow, the stagnant low off to\nour NE will finally get absorbed back into another upper-level\ntrough moving into the Ohio Valley. Once we lose the influence of\nthis low pressure, a more typical summertime pattern will\nestablish itself across the region, with diurnally driven showers\nand thunderstorms becoming the focus for our rain activity.\n\nThankfully, afternoon high temperatures will remain relatively\nstable over the next week, as no upper-level feature is able to\nreally establish itself over the area. Highs will continue to\nrange in the low to mid-90s, with humid conditions pushing heat\nindex values to between 95 and 100 degrees. While heat index\nvalues will be elevated, the need for heat products is currently \nlittle to none, as we expect to remain below critical thresholds \nfor most of the next seven days.\n\n/44/",
